  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💍 Elden Ring Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Tarnished names and boss-worthy titles, in the style of the Lands Between."
    },
    "intro": "Elden Ring's characters are known as much by their titles as their names: Godrick the Grafted, Starscourge Radahn, Rennala, Queen of the Full Moon, Malenia, Blade of Miquella. This **Elden Ring name generator** makes names in those patterns, from a plain Tarnished name for your character to a title worthy of a demigod's boss bar.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Three ways the Lands Between names its great ones",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Name, then title:</strong> Rennala, Queen of the Full Moon; Malenia, Blade of Miquella; Rykard, Lord of Blasphemy; Morgott, the Omen King. The title says what they rule or what they are.</li><li><strong>Name and epithet:</strong> Godrick the Grafted. One word that sums up the horror or the legend.</li><li><strong>Title first:</strong> Starscourge Radahn. A title so famous it comes before the name.</li></ul><p>Your own character, a Tarnished, usually goes by a plain name. The <em>Tarnished name only</em> format gives you one; the others are for the boss you'd like to become, or the one your friends will face in co-op.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What makes a name sound like Elden Ring",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Old European names, slightly worn:</strong> Godfrey, Rennala, Melina, Alexander. Familiar enough to say, strange enough to feel ancient.</li><li><strong>Titles built from the setting's big ideas:</strong> the moon and stars, rot, fire, blood, grafting, the Erdtree.</li><li><strong>Grim honesty:</strong> FromSoftware titles describe exactly what went wrong. A lord of rot is rotting.</li></ul><p>All the names and titles here are new, so you won't accidentally name your character after a demigod.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Naming your Tarnished",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Keep it short for messages.</strong> Your name appears in summon signs and invasions, so a simple name is easier for other players to recognise.</li><li><strong>Save the title for roleplay.</strong> Build a backstory around a title like Warden of the Forsaken Gate, then let the game decide if you live up to it.</li><li><strong>Match the build.</strong> A faith build might suit a golden title; an arcane or bleed build suits something bloodier.</li></ul>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How are Elden Ring boss names made?",
        "answer": "Usually a name plus a title (Rennala, Queen of the Full Moon), a name plus an epithet (Godrick the Grafted) or a title before the name (Starscourge Radahn)."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I name my Tarnished?",
        "answer": "A short, old-sounding name works best, because it shows on summon signs and invasions. Set the format to \"Tarnished name only\" for a list."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are these names from Elden Ring?",
        "answer": "No. They're new names and titles in the game's style."
      }
    ]
  }
